<title>USA: Entergy Miss. nuke seen on line Wednesday.</title>
<headline>Entergy Miss. nuke seen on line Wednesday.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-11-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Entergy Corp's 1,173 megawatt Grand Gulf 1 nuclear power plant will likely resume production Wednesday following scheduled maintenance and refueling, a company spokeswoman said Monday.</p>
<p>&quot;It should synchronize to the grid Wednesday afternoon,&quot; said spokeswoman Diane Park.</p>
<p>The Port Gibson, Miss., plant was shut Oct 19 for the maintenance. If the plant resumes production on Wednesday, the outage will have lasted 38 days.</p>
<p>--New York Power Desk +1 212 859 1627</p>
</text>
